# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Local secrets — never commit the Spicy Lyrics API key.
# Copy .env.example to .env and fill it in; the example file is the committed one.
.env

# Agent / session scratch directories. These are tool state, not app state, and
# one of them (.superpowers/brainstorm/) writes a live session token — committing
# it would publish a credential. Neither belongs in the repository.
.superpowers/
.freebuff/

# The local TTML lyric library: the user's own .ttml files (and its .trash).
# The folder also writes its own .gitignore, so a library elsewhere is covered too.
ttml/

# The Edge WebView2 profile: local storage for the UI's settings, plus the
# browser's own cache. Machine-local and large. Deleting it is how a user resets
# every preference at once (and the app recreates it on the next launch).
.webview/

# PyInstaller output. Both are build products: they are regenerated by
# `python -m PyInstaller PaprikaLyrics.spec` and a committed `dist/` would be 93 MB
# of stale binaries that never match the source beside them.
build/
dist/

# Local runtime cache: contains the user's listening history (track IDs, offsets, lyrics).
# The wildcard also covers hand-made backups (spotify_cache.json.bak), which hold
# the same private data and would otherwise be committed.
spotify_cache.json*
spotify_cache.tmp
*.tmp
